---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../components/seo/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import { siteConfig } from '../config/site';
---
<BaseLayout title="Methodology & Editorial Policy" description={`How ${siteConfig.name} builds converters, cites sources, tests fixtures, and documents limits (E-E-A-T).`} canonicalPath="/methodology/">
  <div class="container content-prose">
    <Breadcrumbs items={[{ name: 'Home', href: '/' }, { name: 'Methodology' }]} />
    <h1>Methodology & editorial policy</h1>
    <div class="answer-box">
      <p>
        We ship working client-side converters, document algorithms and limits in plain language, cite format authorities,
        and never invent star ratings. Pages show published and last-updated dates. Conversion is tested with checked-in
        fixtures under <code>tests/</code> and Vitest.
      </p>
    </div>
    <h2>How tools are built</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Pure conversion functions live under <code>src/lib/converters/</code> with unit tests and fixtures.</li>
      <li>Heavy dependencies (heic2any/WASM, ag-psd, pdf.js, Three.js, etc.) load dynamically after user interaction.</li>
      <li>Known hard problems (full DWG, production MIDI transcription, full FDM slicing) are skipped or scoped with explicit limits on the tool page.</li>
      <li>Library versions are pinned in <code>package.json</code>; upgrades re-run fixtures before release.</li>
    </ul>
    <h2>How conversions are tested</h2>
    <p>
      Each converter has Vitest cases that feed small fixtures (YAML snippets, CSV rows, tiny meshes, sample XML) and assert
      parse success or expected error messages. Image and PDF paths assert blob type / non-empty output where headless
      canvas allows. We do not publish fabricated compression percentages or traffic claims.
    </p>
    <h2>Content standards</h2>
    <p>
      Tool pages include answer-first summaries with a worked example number, methods, mistakes, FAQs (FAQPage schema), and
      sources. Guides expand topical clusters with unique bodies — not copy-pasted operations boilerplate. Governing SEO
      guidance: repository <code>docs/SEO-PLAYBOOK.md</code> and the per-page checklist in
      <code>.cursor/rules/seo-pages.mdc</code>.
    </p>
    <h2>Privacy claims</h2>
    <p>
      “Your file never leaves your device” refers to conversion file bytes: we do not accept uploads for processing. Page
      analytics (GA4 when configured, only after cookie Accept) and future ads are disclosed on
      <a href="/privacy/">Privacy</a> and are separate from document content. We do not claim a service worker or
      offline-after-load guarantee.
    </p>
    <h2>Changelog &amp; corrections</h2>
    <p>
      Material converter or documentation fixes land via pull requests on the public repository. For a factual error on a
      live page, email <a href={`mailto:${siteConfig.contactEmail}`}>{siteConfig.contactEmail}</a> with the URL, the incorrect
      sentence, and a primary source link. We correct the page and bump <code>dateModified</code>.
    </p>
    <p class="meta-row">Last reviewed: <time datetime={siteConfig.lastUpdated}>{siteConfig.lastUpdated}</time></p>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
